{"title":"Career Roadmap · Automation Engineer","role":"Automation Engineer","summary":"An Automation Engineer designs, programs, integrates, commissions, and maintains automated industrial systems. The role sits at the intersection of:","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Instrumentation & Control Engineering"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Automation Engineer designs, programs, integrates, commissions, and maintains automated industrial systems. The role sits at the intersection of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Instrumentation"},{"text":"Control systems"},{"text":"PLC programming"},{"text":"SCADA"},{"text":"Industrial networking"},{"text":"Electrical systems"},{"text":"Robotics"},{"text":"Process control"},{"text":"Industrial IoT"},{"text":"Data acquisition"},{"text":"Manufacturing automation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Instrumentation & Control Engineering is one of the most directly aligned degrees for this career because it provides foundations in sensors, measurement, control theory, process instrumentation, PLCs, industrial electronics, and automation systems."},{"type":"p","text":"A graduate should target entry-level roles such as Automation Engineer, Control Engineer, PLC Programmer, Instrumentation Engineer, SCADA Engineer, or Commissioning Engineer rather than expecting an Automation Manager role immediately after graduation."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"note","label":"2026–2030","text":"Automation & Controls Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong practical knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sensors"},{"text":"Transmitters"},{"text":"Actuators"},{"text":"PLCs"},{"text":"HMI"},{"text":"SCADA"},{"text":"Control systems"},{"text":"Industrial communication"},{"text":"Electrical panels"},{"text":"Motors"},{"text":"Variable-frequency drives"},{"text":"Industrial safety"}]},{"type":"p","tex